          "heading": "England's fifth place at risk if Australia beat All Blacks in Sydney",
          "body": "England are fifth in the World Rugby rankings on 85.68 points, just ahead of Australia on 84.89 as of 16 October. A Wallabies win over the All Blacks in the second Bledisloe Cup Test in Sydney would lift them above England, according to Planet Rugby's permutations, and a margin of more than 15 points would take them past France too. The All Blacks sit second behind South Africa, and their 50-19 win at Eden Park has narrowed that gap to 1.28 points."
